# Security audit allowlist for dev-only dependencies.
# Enforced by .ci/scripts/security/audit.sh (two-pass strategy):
#
#   Pass 1 — production deps (--omit=dev): ZERO TOLERANCE, no allowlist.
#            Any severity → hard fail.
#   Pass 2 — dev deps: this allowlist applies.
#
# Rules:
#   - NEVER add production dependency advisories here; they cannot be allowlisted.
#   - Only add dev-dependency advisories after confirming no upgrade path exists.
#   - Each group MUST have a "# BLOCKER: <reason>" line; the audit script
#     enforces this strictly. Blank lines separate groups.
#
# Currently EMPTY, and that is the correct state. Every previous entry
# (tar, minimatch, yauzl, brace-expansion, tmp, node-tar — 18 advisory IDs
# across 6 groups) was justified by an electron / electron-builder chain.
# Electron is gone from the tree: package-lock.json contains no electron,
# electron-builder, electron-vite, electron-updater, electron-publish,
# app-builder-lib or @electron/* entry, and none of those 18 advisories
# appears in `npm audit` output any more. Do not re-add an entry without
# confirming the advisory actually fires.
#
# 2026-07-31: the brace-expansion GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg entry (id 1124334,
# covering the eslint-vendored 1.1.16 copies via a "<= 5.0.7" affected
# range) was removed: the advisory's affected range narrowed to
# ">= 4.0.0, < 5.0.8" under a new id (1130588), which does not reach 1.x.
# The 1.1.16 copies (eslint, eslint-plugin-import/jsx-a11y/react,
# @eslint/config-array, @eslint/eslintrc) are still in package-lock.json
# unchanged; the advisory itself stopped applying to them, not the tree.
#
# 2026-08-01: id 1130588's own affected range moved AGAIN (npm's advisory
# database re-widened it to "<1.1.17", verified live via `npm audit
# --json`), so it now reaches the same 1.1.16 copies the entry above was
# removed over. Re-added below. This is not a reversal of that removal's
# reasoning -- the underlying fact (no upgrade path exists for these six
# eslint/minimatch@3 edges without crashing eslint) never changed and is
# independently documented in package.json's brace-expansion@^1.1.7
# override BLOCKER comment; only the advisory database's own range
# metadata has been unstable across two consecutive audit windows.

# BLOCKER: brace-expansion GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg (id 1130588, DoS via unbounded
# expansion LENGTH -> OOM). DEV-ONLY: the six eslint/minimatch@3 edges
# (eslint-plugin-import/jsx-a11y/react, @eslint/config-array,
# @eslint/eslintrc, eslint itself) pinned to 1.1.16 by the
# brace-expansion@^1.1.7 override (package.json). NO UPGRADE PATH EXISTS,
# verified rather than assumed: forcing those edges to the root override's
# 5.0.8 crashes eslint, because brace-expansion v5 is ESM-only with a NAMED
# export (`{ expand, EXPANSION_MAX }`) while minimatch@3's
# `var expand = require('brace-expansion'); expand(pattern)` needs the
# callable default export 1.x still provides -- documented verbatim in the
# override's own BLOCKER comment (package.json:250). EXPOSURE: the DoS
# needs attacker-controlled brace patterns; these copies only ever expand
# our own lint globs, in a dev-time tool that is not on any runtime path.
1130588
